-- module `reexp_main` — F3(b) through a RE-EXPORT HOP (`scopes.jsonl`).
-- ⚠️ THE LINE NUMBERS BELOW ARE THE TRANSCRIPT'S CLICK COORDINATES — keep this
-- header exactly 12 lines.
--
-- A DIRECT `import list.*` was already refused, which is exactly what hid this:
-- the arm looked like it worked. A re-exported name is a `DUse`, not a
-- declaration, so the module-source check could not see it and
-- `reexpVal` -> `sortBy` was accepted, breaking the program.
--
-- `intercalate` is the NEGATIVE CONTROL in the same cell: `list` declares it,
-- so the chain COULD reach it, but `reexp_mid` re-exports only `sortBy` — a fix
-- that pulled in everything downstream of the wildcard would refuse it wrongly.
import reexp_mid.*

reexpVal : List Int
reexpVal = [3, 1]

reexpSorted : List Int
reexpSorted = sortBy compare reexpVal
